          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સ્વયંસેવક — svayansevak — \"a volunteer\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "એક સ્વયંસેવકે બાળકોને દૂધ આપ્યું. ek svayansevke bāḷkone dūdh āpyũ. A volunteer gave the children milk."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A masculine or feminine noun, by the person meant."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "સ્વયંસેવક (svayansevak) is built from Sanskrit svayam, \"oneself, of one's own accord\", and sevaka, \"one who serves\" (Monier-Williams): someone who serves of their own will."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
