            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "રાહત — rāhat — \"relief\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "વરસાદ અટક્યો ત્યારે લોકોને રાહત થઈ. varsād aṭakyo tyāre lokone rāhat thaī. When the rain stopped, people felt relieved."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A feminine noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "રાહત (rāhat) is usually traced, through Persian, to Arabic rāḥa, \"rest, ease\". Gujarati uses it for the ease that comes after trouble, રાહત થઈ, and for the help sent to people in need."
            }
          ]
        },
